    "evidence_text": "The Small M\u00fcnsterl\u00e4nder (also SM or Kleiner M\u00fcnsterl\u00e4nder) is a versatile hunting-pointing-retrieving dog breed that reached its current form in the area around M\u00fcnster, Germany.\n\n The Large M\u00fcnsterl\u00e4nder is from the same area, but was developed from different breeding stock and is not related as the names would suggest.\n\n The breed was further developed in Spain, France, Germany, England, and in Italy.\n\nThe Spinone Italiano (] ) is an Italian dog breed.\n\nLarge M\u00fcnsterl\u00e4nder\n\nThe Large M\u00fcnsterl\u00e4nder (or Gro\u00dfer M\u00fcnsterl\u00e4nder) is a breed of gun dog originally from the M\u00fcnster region in Germany.\n\nGerman Longhaired Pointer\n\n Developed in Germany, it is used as a multipurpose gundog.\n\n It is closely related to its cousins, the German Shorthaired Pointer (GSP), the German Wirehaired Pointer (GWP) and the Large M\u00fcnsterl\u00e4nder, which was previously part of the breed.\n\nBracco Italiano\n\nThe Bracco Italiano ] is a breed of dog developed in Italy as a versatile gun dog.\n\nThe Boxer is a medium-sized, short-haired breed of dog, developed in Germany.",
